install.packages(Ncpus > 1) without make

With Ncpus > 1 install.packages() writes a Makefile and runs
`make -k -j`, then `cat` to show a failed package's output. The base
package has no toolchain, so no make: when make is not found, install
one at a time as Ncpus = 1 does, and show the output with readLines().
feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, phase A2.

